BT
/F2 14 Tf 54 735 Td 18 TL
(Abstract) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -28 Td 12 TL
(Beginning with the first-order elimination law c'[t] = k1 c[t], I construct the) Tj T*
(single-dose concentration profile, superpose n doses to obtain a finite geometric) Tj T*
(series, and pass to the limit n -> infinity. The steady-state peak and trough then) Tj T*
(follow by evaluating a single closed form at the two endpoints of one dosing cycle,) Tj T*
(and the finite-n expression reproduces the ManyDoseConcentration function of the) Tj T*
(underlying Mathematica notebooks exactly.) Tj T*
(The derivation reduces to one structural observation: a sum of exponential tails) Tj T*
(offset by equal time steps is a geometric series. Anchoring that sum at the most) Tj T*
(recent dose makes the closed form, its limit, and both clinical extremes follow in) Tj T*
(a few lines of algebra. Elimination is written in base two so the half-life is read) Tj T*
(directly off every formula. Default dosing period: one dose per 24 hours.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 0 -32 Td
(Keywords) Tj
/F1 8 Tf 0 -16 Td 11 TL
(pharmacokinetics; first-order elimination; half-life; absorption ramp; superposition;) Tj T*
(geometric series; steady state; accumulation multiplier; peak; trough; fluctuation) Tj T*
(index; ManyDoseConcentration; closed form; dosing period.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf 0 -35 Td
(Contents) Tj
/F1 8.5 Tf 0 -18 Td 15 TL
(Symbols and standing conventions ........................................ 3) Tj T*
(1  The Elimination Law and Its Half-Life Parameterisation ............... 3) Tj T*
(2  The Single-Dose Concentration Profile ............................... 4) Tj T*
(3  Superposition of n Doses: A Finite Geometric Series ................. 4) Tj T*
(4  The Steady-State Limit ............................................... 5) Tj T*
(5  Peak, Trough, and the Fluctuation Index .............................. 6) Tj T*
(6  Recovering the ManyDoseConcentration Function ........................ 7) Tj T*
(7  Summary and Conclusion ............................................... 7) Tj T*
(Acknowledgements and Sources ............................................. 8) Tj
/F1 8 Tf 190 -55 Td
(Page 2 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
