BT
/F2 13 Tf 54 735 Td 17 TL
(Symbols and standing conventions) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(t = time [h]; h = elimination half-life [h]; x = absorption duration [h];) Tj T*
(P = dosing period [h, default 24]; tau = time since current dose finished absorbing.) Tj T*
(Base-two convention: elimination is written as 2^[-t/h], so after one half-life) Tj T*
(the factor is 1/2, after two it is 1/4, and after m it is 2^[-m].) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 0 -34 Td
(1  The Elimination Law and Its Half-Life Parameterisation) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(A drug is cleared at a rate proportional to the amount present. This first-order) Tj T*
(law is the entire physical input to the model.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Definition 1.1 - First-order elimination law) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 35 -17 Td
(c'[t] = k1 c[t],    k1 < 0.                                      [1]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -35 -19 Td 12 TL
(Proposition 1.2. Every solution has the form) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 35 -16 Td
(c[t] = k2 exp[k1 t].                                               [2]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -35 -18 Td 12 TL
(Separating variables gives dc/c = k1 dt; integrating gives ln|c| = k1 t + const.) Tj T*
(Thus c[t] = k2 exp[k1 t].) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Proposition 1.3 - Half-life reparameterisation) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -16 Td 12 TL
(The half-life h is defined by c[t+h] = [1/2] c[t]. Imposing this on [2] gives) Tj
/F3 8.5 Tf 25 -17 Td
(exp[k1 h] = 1/2  <=>  k1 h = -ln 2  <=>  k1 = -[ln 2]/h.          [3]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -25 -18 Td
(Substituting [3] into [2] gives) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 35 -16 Td
(c[t] = k2 * 2^[-t/h].                                              [4]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -35 -18 Td 12 TL
(Remark 1.4. In base two the half-life is manifest; powers of 2 replace powers of e) Tj T*
(from this point on.) Tj
/F1 8 Tf 190 -55 Td
(Page 3 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
