BT
/F2 13 Tf 54 735 Td 17 TL
(2  The Single-Dose Concentration Profile) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(An oral dose is not absorbed instantaneously. Over an absorption window of length x) Tj T*
(the drug enters the blood at a constant rate; afterwards [4] governs its decay.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Definition 2.1 - Single-dose profile, normalised to unit concentration at t = x) Tj
/F3 8.3 Tf 15 -17 Td 11 TL
(c_single[t] = t/x,                 0 < t <= x;) Tj T*
(c_single[t] = 2^[-[t-x]/h],        t > x.                           [5]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -15 -18 Td 12 TL
(The profile satisfies c_single[0] = 0 and c_single[x] = 1 and is continuous at t=x.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Definition 2.3 - Finish-of-absorption time) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 45 -16 Td
(t_k = [k-1]P + x.                                                   [6]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -45 -18 Td
(For t > t_k the residual tail of dose k is) Tj
/F3 8.5 Tf 15 -16 Td
(c_k[t] = 2^[-[t-t_k]/h] = 2^[-[t-x-[k-1]P]/h].                    [7]) Tj
/F2 13 Tf -15 -31 Td
(3  Superposition of n Doses: A Finite Geometric Series) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(Equation [1] is linear, so contributions add. After n doses, at a time t in the) Tj T*
(elimination phase of the current cycle,) Tj
/F3 8.5 Tf 10 -17 Td
(C_n[t] = sum[k=1..n] 2^[-[t-x-[k-1]P]/h].                          [8]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -10 -18 Td
(Form A - anchored at the first dose:) Tj
/F3 8.2 Tf 5 -16 Td 11 TL
(C_n[t] = 2^[-[t-x]/h] sum[j=0..n-1] [2^[P/h]]^j) Tj T*
(       = 2^[-[t-x]/h] [2^[nP/h]-1]/[2^[P/h]-1].                   [9]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -5 -18 Td 12 TL
(Here the ratio 2^[P/h] is greater than 1: measured from the first dose, later terms) Tj T*
(are larger. Form A is the expression implemented in the notebooks.) Tj
/F1 8 Tf 190 -50 Td
(Page 4 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
