stream
BT
/F2 12 Tf 54 735 Td 16 TL
(3  Superposition of n Doses - continued) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(Let tau be elapsed time since the current dose finished absorbing:) Tj
/F3 8.5 Tf 20 -16 Td
(tau = t - t_n = t - x - [n-1]P,    0 <= tau <= P-x.              [10]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -20 -18 Td
(Re-index [8] by i=n-k, cycles into the past. Then Form B is) Tj
/F3 8.2 Tf 5 -16 Td 11 TL
(C_n[tau] = sum[i=0..n-1] 2^[-[tau+iP]/h]) Tj T*
(         = 2^[-tau/h] sum[i=0..n-1] r^i,   r := 2^[-P/h], 0<r<1. [11]) Tj T*
(C_n[tau] = 2^[-tau/h] [1-r^n]/[1-r]) Tj T*
(         = 2^[-tau/h] [1-2^[-nP/h]]/[1-2^[-P/h]].                [12]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -5 -22 Td 12 TL
(The two forms agree after substituting t=[n-1]P+x+tau into [9]. Only Form B has a) Tj T*
(finite n -> infinity limit because it holds tau fixed inside the current cycle.) Tj T*
(Mixing the prefactor of one form with the ratio of the other is the algebraic trap.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 0 -32 Td
(4  The Steady-State Limit) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(Since 0<r<1, r^n = 2^[-nP/h] -> 0. Therefore) Tj
/F3 8.5 Tf 15 -17 Td 11 TL
(C_inf[tau] = 2^[-tau/h]/[1-2^[-P/h]]) Tj T*
(           = 2^[[P-tau]/h]/[2^[P/h]-1].                          [13]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -15 -18 Td
(Written as the tails of all past doses,) Tj
/F3 8 Tf 5 -16 Td 11 TL
(C_inf[tau] = 2^[-tau/h] + 2^[-[tau+P]/h] + 2^[-[tau+2P]/h] + ...) Tj T*
(           = 2^[-tau/h]/[1-2^[-P/h]].                            [14]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -5 -20 Td 12 TL
(The accumulation multiplier is [1-2^[-P/h]]^-1 = 2^[P/h]/[2^[P/h]-1].) Tj T*
(If h >> P there is strong accumulation; if h << P the multiplier tends to 1.) Tj
/F1 8 Tf 190 -55 Td
(Page 5 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
