BT
/F2 13 Tf 54 735 Td 17 TL
(5  Peak, Trough, and the Fluctuation Index) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 0 -22 Td 12 TL
(Formula [13] decreases monotonically in tau, so the steady-state extremes occur at) Tj T*
(the endpoints of tau in [0,P-x].) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Theorem 5.1 - Steady-state peak, at tau = 0) Tj
/F3 8.4 Tf 10 -17 Td 11 TL
(peak_ss = C_inf[0] = 1/[1-2^[-P/h]]) Tj T*
(        = 2^[P/h]/[2^[P/h]-1] = 1 + 1/[2^[P/h]-1].               [15]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -10 -18 Td 12 TL
(The 1 is the dose just absorbed; the remaining term is everything left from prior) Tj T*
(doses.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Theorem 5.2 - Steady-state trough, at tau = P-x) Tj
/F3 8.4 Tf 10 -17 Td 11 TL
(trough_ss = C_inf[P-x] = 2^[-[P-x]/h]/[1-2^[-P/h]]) Tj T*
(          = 2^[x/h]/[2^[P/h]-1].                                 [16]) Tj
/F2 9 Tf -10 -18 Td
(Corollary 5.3 - Fluctuation index) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 35 -17 Td
(peak_ss / trough_ss = 2^[[P-x]/h].                                [17]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -35 -20 Td 12 TL
(The swing depends only on how many half-lives fit into the gap P-x between the end) Tj T*
(of absorption and the next dose. Larger x or smaller P flattens the profile; a short) Tj T*
(half-life sharpens it.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf 0 -18 Td
(Proposition 5.4 - Agreement with notebook definitions, P = 24) Tj
/F3 8.1 Tf 5 -17 Td 11 TL
(trough_min[x,h] = 2^[x/h]/[2^[24/h]-1].                            [18]) Tj T*
(peak_max[x,h] = 1/[2^[24/h]-1] + [[12+x-12 ceil[x/24]] ceil[x/24]]/x. [19]) Tj
/F1 9 Tf -5 -20 Td 12 TL
(For 0<x<=24, ceil[x/24]=1, so the second term in [19] reduces to 1 and [19]) Tj T*
(becomes exactly [15]. The ceiling expression generalises x>P.) Tj
/F1 8 Tf 190 -55 Td
(Page 6 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
